<https://linked.data.gov.au/def/alum/1.1> prez:description "Tertiary classes 1.1.1-1.1.6 are based on the Collaborative Australian Protected Areas Database (CAPAD) classification (Cresswell and Thomas 1997). These classes can also be translated from the International Union for Conservation of Nature Guidelines for applying protected area management categories (IUCN 2008)."@en ;
	prez:label "Nature conservation"@en .

<https://linked.data.gov.au/def/alum/3.2> prez:description "Pasture and forage production, both annual and perennial, based on significant active modification or replacement of the initial vegetation. For ALUM purposes, this class is used when there is greater than 50 per cent dominant exotic species while 2.1, - Grazing native vegetation, is applied when there is greater than 50 per cent dominant native species. Most jurisdictions have datasets specifically designed to distinguish native from non-native vegetation. These datasets should be used to report on native versus non-native vegetation, as the ALUM Classification maps the actual land use as a priority over land cover.Land under pasture at the time of mapping may be in a rotation system, so that at another time the same area may be, for example, under cropping. Land in a rotation system should be classified according to the prime use (if known) or the land use at the time of mapping, with rotation information recorded in the management field. If the rotation sequence is known record this in the comments field. Effort should be made to distinguish a land use change from a rotation."@en ;
	prez:label "Grazing modified pastures"@en .

emsa-cv:032a1c8b-1048-5c81-bd06-8afce5c12451 prez:description "Type of Landform Element with a slope built-up or eroded by the wind (similar to a Dune)." ;
	prez:label "Dune slope" .

emsa-cv:077edbc4-8980-5e85-a6eb-1f4bd3aa1bbf prez:description "Type of Landform Element with a large, water-filled closed depression." ;
	prez:label "Lake" .

emsa-cv:09f2d5d6-21b7-5e0d-b3c4-aad508a27e00 prez:description "Alluvial plain characterised by frequently active erosion and aggradation by channelled or overbank stream flow, unless otherwise specified; 'frequently active' is to mean that flow has an Average Recurrence Interval of 50 years or less. Included types of landform pattern are: bar plain; meander plain; covered plain; anastomotic plain. Related relict landform patterns are: stagnant alluvial plain; terrace; terraced land (partly relict)." ;
	prez:label "Floodplain" .

emsa-cv:30bd2063-582d-5156-8ea0-faab8d16b102 prez:description "Type of Landform Element that has very gently inclined to steep crest; smoothly convex; eroded mainly by creep and sheet wash. A typical element of mountains; hills; low hills and rises." ;
	prez:label "Hillcrest" .

emsa-cv:484d51eb-c1ee-597c-aed0-664a28e7b1d1 prez:description "Refers to the NVIS dominant vegetation structural formation class, with a percent cover of about 0.25-20% of tree mallee (e.g., certain individuals of Eucalypts multistemmed from base). " ;
	prez:label "Open mallee woodland" .

emsa-cv:517d2f98-9d24-5b68-b8d8-f5393eba310a prez:description "Refers to the NVIS dominant vegetation structural formation class, with a percent cover of about 50-80% members of Heath (e.g., Ericaceae, Myrtaceae). " ;
	prez:label "Heathland" .

emsa-cv:5459d7c1-b29f-4616-9572-f2f323520cfc prez:description "Plant growth characterised as completely flat on the substrate, including trailing plants." ;
	prez:label "prostrate" .

emsa-cv:565511a8-c50b-53fb-8f59-995e52a01ed2 prez:description "Other types of liquid preservative used to store invertebrate samples.", "Refers to any 'other' categorical collection NOT listed in the collection.", "Refers to the any Other type of substrate/s used for fauna signs-based observation.", "Represents any 'Other' categorical collection NOT listed in the given collection." ;
	prez:label "Other (specify)" .

emsa-cv:56dff2fb-9cc0-5262-8d70-15e383f88ab7 prez:description "Trees: Mixed size and age classes, usually identified by two or more strata dominated by the same species but can also be sites with different species regenerating in the understorey of an older canopy; Shrubs: Mixed size and age classes; usually two or more strata dominated by the same species but includes sites with different species regenerating in the understorey of an older canopy; Grasses and herbs: A mixture of mature, perennial and immature annual species present on site; Cryptograms: A mixture of mature reproductive plants with immature regeneration." ;
	prez:label "uneven age" .

emsa-cv:57be29f6-1c6a-5c4d-89f2-00b21d4f4178 prez:description "Any ecological impacts caused by an introduced species, alien species, exotic species, or non-native species directly or indirectly on a native species and its ecological niche." ;
	prez:label "introduced plant species impact" .

emsa-cv:5c7e64fc-188c-5d94-b727-c88458bc7f95 prez:description "Type of Landform Element with a crest built-up or eroded by the wind." ;
	prez:label "Dune crest" .

emsa-cv:5cd65691-a295-577c-9f94-cd4756337e3f prez:description "Type of Landform Element which is elongated; gently curved; low ridge built up by wind on the margin of a playa; typically with a moderate; wave-modified slope towards the playa and a gentle outer slope." ;
	prez:label "Lunette" .

emsa-cv:7d1b555a-0c69-42d7-9ffc-e615bad1cc43 prez:description "Refers to the Major Vegetation Groups (MVG) as identified by the National Vegetation Information System (NVIS)." ;
	prez:label "Eucalypt Open Woodlands" .

emsa-cv:7ecfb199-be34-5656-887b-c6205faf0cd1 prez:description "Refers to the NVIS dominant vegetation structural formation class, with a percent cover of about 0.25-20% of shrubs, including cycad, grass-tree, tree-fern. " ;
	prez:label "Sparse shrubland" .

emsa-cv:804d7021-ff30-5c53-86ec-17d65cf46cb9 prez:description "Refers to the Major Vegetation Groups (MVG) as identified by the National Vegetation Information System (NVIS)." ;
	prez:label "Mallee Woodlands and Shrublands" .

emsa-cv:a80fd3dd-894e-5ad6-a2dc-b7e82e26baa5 prez:description "Level landform pattern with extremely low relief. The shallow to deep alluvial stream channels are sparse to widely spaced; forming a unidirectional; integrated network. There may be frequently active erosion and aggradation by channelled and overbank stream flow; or the landforms may be relict from these processes. Included types of landform pattern are: Flood plain; Bar plain; Meander plain; Covered plain; Anastomotic plain; Delta; Stagnant alluvial plain; Terrace; Terraced land." ;
	prez:label "Alluvial plain" .

emsa-cv:c94a751a-13d2-5840-b147-928c89ed1d7b prez:description "Type of Landform Element with a hillock built up by human activity." ;
	prez:label "Landform Element- Mound" .

emsa-cv:dc1bdfa6-5315-5b03-bd00-6b8cd4ebb256 prez:description "Lithology of soil with an unidentified, unconsolidated material." ;
	prez:label "Unconsolidated material (unidentified)" .

emsa-cv:dd035eed-24b2-41b5-a3cc-7270c2c590b5 prez:description "Any notes related to the observations made during the survey." ;
	prez:label "observation notes" .

emsa-cv:df842727-5c00-4758-993e-3bb1558afa43 prez:description "Plants with growth characterised of many stems growing in clusters attached at the base." ;
	prez:label "tufted" .

emsa-cv:f0e21988-4659-5de2-aa77-9d4112ead940 prez:description "Landform pattern of very low relief (9-30 m) and very gentle to steep slopes. The fixed; erosional stream channels are closely to very widely spaced and form a non directional to convergent; integrated or interrupted tributary pattern. The pattern is eroded by continuously active to barely active creep and sheet flow." ;
	prez:label "Rises" .

emsa-cv:f125acdb-8cf9-53f6-b02f-38afd3cb2155 prez:description "A description of the type of disturbance in a study plot." ;
	prez:label "Highly disturbed" .

emsa-cv:f3875738-25f3-5d54-8877-afebc97fd891 prez:description "Trees: Dominated by small, juvenile, dense to very sparse regenerating plants, with or without a few older, widely spaced, emergent plants; Shrubs: Dominated by small, juvenile, dense to very sparse regenerating plants. A few older, widely spaced emergents may be present; Grasses and herbs: Plants small and juvenile stages predominate, bare soil or old litter common; Cryptograms: Thin growth of young plants or widely spaced clumps of young plants." ;
	prez:label "early regeneration" .

emsa-cv:f505c960-4d90-52f6-aee5-18102b784746 prez:description "A description of the type of disturbance in a study plot." ;
	prez:label "None except HEAVY grazing by hoofed animals" .

emsa-cv:f9f75088-5788-5af5-9398-2f24f411ec6b prez:description "Refers to the NVIS dominant vegetation structural formation class, with a percent cover of about 0-5% members of trees including palms." ;
	prez:label "Isolated clumps of trees" .

