                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                <a  href="#appendices">Appendix</a>
                                            </li>
                                        </ol>
                                        <h1  id="standard-protocol">Standard Protocol</h1>
                                        <h2  id="field-collection-1">Field Collection</h2>
                                        <h3  id="pre-requisites-1">Pre-requisites</h3>
                                        <p>Pre-requisites for completing this protocol:</p>
                                        <ul>
                                            <li>
                                                <p>Generate area checklists from Atlas of Living Australia,Australasian Virtual Herbarium or herbaria electronic floras, includingknown, threatened, and sensitive species from the project area.</p>
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                <p>Become familiar with the characters and habitat requirements ofthreatened and sensitive species potentially occurring in the projectarea.</p>
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                <p>Become familiar with the TERN Vascular Plant CollectionGuidelines.</p>
                                            </li>
                                        </ul>
                                        <h3  id="time-estimate">Time estimate</h3>
                                        <p>Survey time requirements will vary depending on the number andexperience of personnel, their familiarity with the flora of the region,the species richness and cover within the plot, and the number of plantspecimen vouchers versus plant photo vouchers required.</p>
                                        <p>As a general guide:</p>
                                        <ul>
                                            <li>
                                                <p>Allow between 0.5–1.5 hours to search for flora species andcollect plant specimen and plant photo vouchers from the plot.</p>
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                <p>Allow between 0.5–1 hour to prepare plant specimen vouchers,attach voucher labels, enter and scan the species into the app, andtransfer the specimens to a field press.</p>
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                <p>Allow approximately 10 minutes per field press, every 2–3 daysduring the field survey, to inspect and change newspaper ifnecessary.</p>
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                <p>Allow 1–2 hours after the field survey to deliver the plantspecimen vouchers to the local State or Territory herbarium.</p>
                                            </li>
                                        </ul>
                                        <h3  id="personnel-requirements-1">Personnel requirements</h3>
                                        <p>Number of personnel and skills:</p>
                                        <ul>
                                            <li>
                                                <p>Searching the plot and collecting a plant specimen voucher orplant photo voucher for all flora species present is best conducted withtwo personnel, one collecting plant specimens and the other recordingplant photo vouchers directly into the app. This also enables moreground, including microhabitats, to be covered from multipleviewpoints.</p>
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                <p>Processing plant specimen vouchers is best conducted with twopersonnel, one processing the specimens and one recording the datadirectly into the app.</p>
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                <p>The surveyors making the observations should be familiar with andexperienced in identifying the flora species of the region. If surveyorsare not confident, time should be dedicated to practising, using fieldreference guides, and seeking advice before conducting thisprotocol.</p>
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                <p>Floristics surveys involve the collection of plant specimenvouchers. Therefore, scientific permits are likely to be required.Additional permits may be required for collecting threatened floraspecies, so always check with your local authority.</p>
                                            </li>
                                        </ul>"""^^rdf:HTML ;
	prez:label "Floristics - Standard Protocol" .

emsa-cv:dd551efe-9dcd-5c46-8735-8f4642e03f5a prez:description "Slope descriptor representing a slope angle in the range from between 1°46' - 5°45' degree." ;
	prez:label "Gently inclined" .

emsa-cv:ffb1c491-bbb1-5823-ac03-0543f9a9627a prez:description "The method of bird sighting in the form of calls, or acoustic signals. ", "The method of fauna sighting in the form of calls, or acoustic signals. " ;
