emsa-cv:3dc4bc55-b40a-5ed9-94ba-697d59489e67 prez:description "Refers to the spatial point location, denoting the 'North East' corner of the study plot.", "The spatial point location which represents the cardinal direction at the 'northeast' corner of the study plot." ;
	prez:label "plot corner - North East" .

emsa-cv:8457585c-9358-5bc0-b975-0a449b304006 prez:description "A description of the type of disturbance in a study plot." ;
	prez:label "None except LIGHT grazing by hoofed animals" .

emsa-cv:afa07308-191b-5daf-a106-c3208a477155 prez:description "Refers to the spatial point location, denoting the 'South West' corner of the study plot.", "The spatial point location which represents the cardinal direction at the 'southwest' corner of the study plot." ;
	prez:label "plot corner - South West" .

emsa-cv:cd03aa9a-1221-5db9-99e7-800cba375db3 prez:description "Trees: Mature-sized plants, with or without emergent senescent plants. Trees at maximum height for the type and conditions. Crown at full lateral development and limbs thicker in stands. No apical dominance; Shrubs: Mature-sized plants with or without emergent senescent plants; Grasses and herbs: Most plants of reproductive age; depending on vegetation type, reproduction evident, or would be if environmental conditions were appropriate (e.g., water availability); Cryptograms: Swards of plants common; plants of mature physiognomy (clump sizes and forms); reproduction common at appropriate times of year or drought/rain cycle; overall health and vigour high." ;
	prez:label "mature phase" .

emsa-cv:e813ea59-6a6d-50fe-b7c1-d449dbb2a982 prez:description "A plant phenological stage, characterised by abundance of young or developing unopened buds, indicating an onset for flowering." ;
	prez:label "phenological stage - buds" .

tern-cv:8282fb22-4135-415c-8ca2-317860d102fb prez:description "Most of the attributes for land surface deal with its physical properties (e.g. aspect, elevation). Some other reflect properties within (e.g. microrelief). Some attributes reflect the influence of present or past land use practice (e.g. disturbance of site, erosion).", "Surface layer of Earth which is primarily composed of solid material and is not covered by oceans or other bodies of water." ;
	prez:label "land surface"@en .

