emsa-cv:5488c9ea-e3a2-5348-887b-065d29b848ab prez:description "Refers to any categorical values/attributes that are 'Not Applicable' to a particular observation in the study.", "Target fauna species." ;
	prez:label "Not Applicable" .

emsa-cv:9d312ae3-31e2-5479-b138-e59080daa837 prez:description "Indicates the position 3 of the photopoint position location." ;
	prez:label "photopoint position- 3" .

emsa-cv:a8db263e-7a39-5b85-a5d2-8e1af7ce1e39 prez:description "Refers to NO recognised method of observation stated for a target fauna." ;
	prez:label "no stated method" .

emsa-cv:a924aa29-9d96-5419-8cd3-a72365532000 prez:description "Indicates the position 2 of the photopoint position location." ;
	prez:label "photopoint position- 2" .

emsa-cv:c77cde17-dfd8-5513-adaa-1c3f1d3fa055 prez:description "Indicates the position 1 of the photopoint position location." ;
	prez:label "photopoint position- 1" .

emsa-cv:d16cfca2-ac22-58f8-9142-8703bd45931e prez:description "Plot dimensions - equivalent to 1 hectare." ;
	prez:label "plot dimension- 100m x 100m" .

tern-cv:2361dea8-598c-4b6f-a641-2b98ff199e9e prez:description "An animal occurrence is a sample of an animal or group of animals at a particular point and time. Unlike animal individuals, an animal occurrence may not specifically relate to a distinct physical entity (e.g. a specific animal individual), but provides a sample which may come from an individuals or a group.", "An existence of an animal or group of animals sampled at a particular place at a particular time." ;
	prez:label "animal occurrence"@en .

tern-cv:ea3a4c64-dac3-4660-809a-8ad5ced8997b prez:description "Group of plants representing multiple species living in a specified place and time.", "Theoretically, it is useful to consider the complete set of plants belonging to all species living in a particular place and time as plant community (community sensu lato see Vellend 2016). In practice, studies often focus on a subset of the whole plant community chosen on the basis of growth form, taxonomy or particular interactions (Morin 2011)." ;
	prez:label "plant community"@en .

<https://linked.data.gov.au/dataset/bdr/cfeb6552-abf6-4fc2-9fe1-d62f76c8579f/submission/333ef2dd-785a-45b0-a99d-2fa4c72c22d8/phenomenon-time/31ec6fc2-9c84-b903-d042-d17f4d1a14e4> a time:Instant ;
